<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 2.x Task//EN" "task.dtd">
<task id="to_create_a_save_map_for_display_map_fields_1b9a6b" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>To create a Save Map for Display Map Fields</title>
   <shortdesc>Click on the placeholder arrow icon in the upper right-hand corner and choose an option</shortdesc>
   <prolog>
      <author type="creator">Rakesh Singh</author>
       <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>Save</keyword>
        <keyword>Display</keyword>
        <keyword>clicks</keyword>
        <keyword>placeholder</keyword>
        <keyword>Click</keyword>
        <keyword>Danny</keyword>
        <indexterm>Save</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Display</indexterm>
        <indexterm>clicks</indexterm>
      </keywords>
          <prodinfo>
        <prodname/>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <taskbody>
      <steps>
         <step>
            <cmd>From the X-Author ribbon, click <b>Save Map</b>.</cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>98668101</title>
                  <image href="../attachments/98667692/98668101.png" width="405" height="158" placement="break">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Click <b>Create</b>. The Save Map panel opens in Excel.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>In the Name field, enter a name for your Save Map. Pick a name that makes it easy to distinguish from your other Save Maps.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Click <b>Add Display Map Fields</b>.</cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>98668091</title>
                  <image href="../attachments/98667692/98668091.png" width="636" height="486" placement="break">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
            <info>
               <note type="tip">
                  <p>Click on the <image href="../attachments/98667692/98668090.png" placement="inline" width="16" height="14">
                           <alt>placeholder</alt>
                        </image>
                      arrow icon in the upper right-hand corner and choose an option to move or resize the Save Map panel.</p>
               </note>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Use the <b>Filter by</b> drop-down to filter the list of fields for a specific Display Map.</cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>190354474</title>
                  <image href="../attachments/98667692/190354474.png" width="339" height="113" placement="break">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Select the fields to add to your Save Map, and click <b>Apply</b>. Click <b>Select All</b> if you want to choose all Display Map fields.</cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>190354475</title>
                  <image href="../attachments/98667692/190354475.png" width="599" height="509" placement="break">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Click <b>Save</b>.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Click <b>Close</b>.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Click <b>Save App</b>.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Danny connects to his environment and opens the Sales Pipeline app.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>He clicks <b>Save Map</b> and clicks <b>Create </b>to start a new Display Map.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Danny enters the name "Save Pipeline" and clicks <b>Add Display Map Fields</b>.</cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>98668089</title>
                  <image href="../attachments/98667692/98668089.png" width="684" height="148" placement="break">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Danny decides that all of the Opportunity fields should be enabled for saving back to his environment. He clicks <b>Select All</b> and clicks <b>Apply</b>.</cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>190354477</title>
                  <image href="../attachments/98667692/190354477.png" width="601" height="525" placement="break">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Danny clicks <b>Save</b> to save the map and clicks <b>Close</b>.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Danny clicks <b>Save App</b> to save all changes to the app.</cmd>
         </step>
      </steps>
      <result>
         <p>Use Case: Sales Pipeline Save Map</p>
         <p>Danny Designer is designing an app with Account, Opportunity and User objects for sales persons to use to manage their sales pipeline. He has created a Display Map to link data from his environment to the cells in the Excel workbook and now needs to create a Save Map for saving data back to his environment.</p>
         <p>Danny takes the following steps to create a Save Map:</p>
      </result>
   </taskbody>
</task>